# The OS server's stacks (roadmap os-server.md P5, P12): each of its threads
# has 1 KB of its data segment, filled at its first start; after the
# deepest calls the processes make - a directory of two clusters, a file
# through the FAT, a cd, ps, a fault reported - the deepest of them has a
# quarter of its part or more to spare, as the server says at each exit
# (TEST_OS_STACKS).
program: sh
define: TEST_OS_STACKS
install: C /BIN/PS z-ps.rx
install: C /BIN/CRASH z-crash.rx
keys: ls -l b:/many\ncat c:/docs/hello.txt\ncd c:/docs\nps -e\ncrash gp\nexit\n
match: contains
timeout: 120
emulators: bochs mame
---
/c/DOCS$ exit
os: a thread's stack: a quarter of it or more to spare: yes
